    "wikipedia_summary": "<i><b>Cocculus laurifolius</b></i>, the <b>laurel-leaved snail tree</b>, is a medium-sized tree of the genus <i>Cocculus</i>. It is native to Japan and China. It commonly grows to the height of 40 to 60 ft, with a spread of 20 to 40 ft. Form is round headed with a medium to fast growth rate and a coarse texture. Leaves are simple, Large (6 to 12 inches) with a whorled bud arrangement. Leaf color is medium green with a fall color of...",
